-- title:
--   G Hat Facts Of Self Consistency And Commutation
-- statement:
--   **Self-consistency and commutation hypotheses produce the two G-hat facts.**
--
--   Let $\psi$ be a bipartite quantum state and let $G^x$ be a slice-indexed family of projective polynomial submeasurements. Assume $0\le\gamma$, $\gamma\le1$, $0\le\zeta$, $\zeta\le1$, and $d\le q$. Suppose the complete and incomplete parts of the family each satisfy their required self-consistency relation at error $\zeta$, and their required commutation relation at errors $\gamma$ and $\zeta$. Then the completed G-hat family has both of the following properties.
--
--   First, its left- and right-placed outcome families are related under the uniform slice-height distribution by the state-dependent squared-distance bound
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SDDRel}_{\psi,\operatorname{Unif}(\mathbb{F}_q)}(\widehat G_{\mathrm{left}},\widehat G_{\mathrm{right}};2\zeta).
--   $$
--
--   Second, its left- and right-placed pair-product families are related under the uniform distribution on pairs of slice heights by
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SDDOpRel}_{\psi,\operatorname{Unif}(\mathbb{F}_q^2)}
--   \left(\widehat G_{\mathrm{pair,left}},\widehat G_{\mathrm{pair,right}};
--   138m\left(\operatorname{rpow}(\gamma,1/16)+\operatorname{rpow}(\zeta,1/16)+\operatorname{rpow}(d/q,1/16)\right)\right).
--   $$
--
--   Thus the four component estimates combine into the self-consistency and commutation conclusions for the completed slice family.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.gHatFacts_ofSelfConsistencyAndCommutation`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
